ation-verification step and the causal patching test (Exp 5) mitigate this, and a graded result remains informative.", 'Recitation and execution representations may be entangled rather than separable; the steering/patching tests, not probe onset alone, are decisive, and partial dissociation would weaken the strong claim while still being informative.', "Defining a single 'execution-state' representation is hard when procedures are multi-step and distributed; primary analysis restricts to procedures with a localizable branch/decision point and reports coverage.", 'The binding intervention could break correctly-executed procedures or degrade fluency if the injected direction overlaps useful features; the both-correct and unrelated-procedure specificity controls are central and utility may be capped.', 'A single transferable binding vector may not exist if coupling is procedure-specific, limiting practical generality though still scientifically informative.', 'Multi-token outputs and long procedures complicate readout; primary analysis restricts to short outputs / single decision points with reported coverage.', 'Findings on 6–8B models may not transfer to frontier-scale models beyond an academic budget.']}

