scalar-based prediction. Define shortcut-decided comparisons as those where the answer diverges from the scalar prediction or the scalar margin is near zero while the answer is confident. Test (regression/AUROC) whether transitivity violations concentrate on shortcut-decided, small-scalar-margin comparisons, controlling for entity frequency and lexical similarity.", '5. Causal test via patching/steering: (a) Force scalar-based reading: patch the comparison-answer position to be driven by the scalar-subspace difference (inject the scalar projections of both entities computed in isolation) and test whether the answer flips to the scalar-correct value and whether transitivity is restored across the triple. (b) Suppress the pairwise-shortcut direction (learned low-rank difference between shortcut-decided and scalar-decided matched states) and re-measure. (c) Reverse control: amplify the shortcut direction to induce violations on demand. Metrics: per-triple transitivity-restoration rate; comparison accuracy on shortcut-decided pairs.', "6. Repair intervention with specificity: Apply the scalar-reading steering/shortcut-suppression on held-out triples with dose control. Metrics: transitivity-violation reduction; comparison-accuracy gain on shortcut-decided pairs; specificity (accuracy on scalar-decided pairs the model already gets right must not drop; accuracy on 200 unrelated non-comparison facts pre/post); fluency (held-out perplexity). Baselines: a 'reason step by step / recall each value first' re-prompt, ROME editing of individual attribute values (expected not to help), and a random-direction control.", '7. Transfer and generality: Test whether a single scalar-reading/shortcut-suppression recipe generalizes across attributes (train on birth-year comparisons, apply to elevation/population); repeat core analyses (2-6) on Llama-3-8B, Mistral-7B, Qwen2.5-7B; report whether larger models rely more on the scalar subspace (fewer violations).', "8. Source analysis: Regress 