less. Regress override rate on slot position, placeholder-vs-correct frequency gap (is the placeholder the more typical/frequent value?), and inter-slot semantic relatedness, to quantify whether override is driven by premature commitment to the category-typical value (the core mechanistic claim).'], 'Risk Factors and Limitations': ['Position-dependent errors could arise from generic long-generation degradation or attention dilution rather than a specific stale-placeholder mechanism; the isolated-query control, permuted-order design (same fact early vs late), and the ahead-of-time placeholder decoding (Exp 4) are the decisive separators, and length controls are included.', 'The prefetched placeholder and the correct-value signal may be entangled; the causal patching/suppression tests (Exp 5), not probe AUROC alone, are decisive, and graded results remain informative.', "Verifying a fact is 'stored' via isolated recall risks overestimation from format effects; conservative content-probe thresholds and first-slot recall as an additional check with reported coverage mitigate this.", 'Suppression could corrupt earlier correct slots or degrade fluency; the earlier-slot and unrelated-fact specificity controls (Exp 6) are central and utility may be capped even if the analysis holds.', 'Override may be rare relative to genuine ignorance for some attributes; the paired within-subject early-vs-late design maximizes power and a modest but significant position effect is still informative.', 'A single transferable intervention recipe may not exist if prefetching is relation-specific, limiting practical generality though still scientifically informative.', 'Ahead-of-time decoding is noisiest when slots are close together; primary analysis uses prompts with clear inter-slot separation and single-token-first answers, with reported coverage.', 'Findings on 7-9B models may not transfer to frontier-scale models beyond an academic budget.']}

