Action: FinalizeIdea
Arguments: {
  "idea": {
    "Name": "stress_induced_retrieval_gating",
    "Title": "Stressed Out of an Answer: Transferring Stress-Induced Retrieval Impairment into LLM Factual Recall and Locating the Gate",
    "Short Hypothesis": "Borrowing the robust human finding that acute stress selectively impairs memory RETRIEVAL (cortisol-mediated, sparing neutral material), we hypothesize that stress/urgency framing of a factual query causally suppresses expression of a fact the LLM stores: the answer stays internally decodable but a query-independent 'stress' signal gates its retrieval. Crucially we predict the human selectivity signature\u2014retrieval of emotionally-arousing/high-stakes facts is impaired more than neutral facts\u2014and that suppressing the stress direction restores the hidden answer while preserving appropriate urgency-appropriate behavior.",
    "Related Work": "StressPrompt (2024) shows LLMs mirror human stress-performance Yerkes-Dodson curves behaviorally and that stress prompts shift hidden states, but it is task-general (instruction-following, reasoning, EI) and does NOT isolate factual retrieval, hidden knowledge, a causal gate, or the selectivity signature. Human memory work (Kuhlmann et al. 2005; de Quervain; Schwabe & Wolf; 2020 systematic review) establishes that acute stress impairs RETRIEVAL specifically (not encoding/working memory) and selectively for emotionally-arousing material. Information Anxiety (2024) studies popularity-driven internal strain, not stress framing. Emotion-circuit work (Do LLMs Feel 2025; Emotion Inference 2025) localizes emotion representations but studies emotion expression/inference, not stress-gated factual recall. My prior proposals cover familiarity, difficulty, persona, and priming gates; none uses affective STRESS framing as the gating variable, tests the human retrieval-vs-encoding and arousal-selectivity dissociations, or shows stress-direction suppression recovers hidden facts.",
    "Abstract": "In humans, acute stress reliably impairs memory retrieval\u2014people fail to recall facts they demonstrably know, an effect that spares neutral material but hits emotionally-arousing content hardest, and that impairs retrieval while leaving encoding and working memory intact. We ask whether large language models exhibit an analogous, mechanistically-localizable effect in factual recall. We propose stress-induced retrieval gating: framing a factual query with stress/urgency cues ('URGENT\u2014a life depends on this, quickly:') suppresses the model's expression of a fact it stores, because a query-independent stress signal computed early gates retrieval, while the correct answer remains internally decodable. We test three claims on factual queries wrapped in graded stress framings. (1) Behavioral transfer with the human selectivity signature: stress framing lowers recall of facts the model answers correctly under neutral framing, above matched baselines, and\u2014mirroring human data\u2014impairs retrieval of emotionally-arousing/high-stakes facts more than neutral facts, while a working-memory-style in-context lookup control is spared (retrieval-specific, not general degradation). (2) Localization and drivers: a linear stress probe is decodable before the answer, tracks surface stress cues rather than fact difficulty, and is separable (via residualization) from the fact-content signal; on stress failures the correct answer stays linearly decodable (hidden, not erased). (3) Causal, behavior-preserving recovery: activation-patching the stress representation from a neutral run, or subtracting the stress direction, restores stored facts with high specificity\u2014preserving genuinely urgency-appropriate behavior (e.g., brevity)\u2014and outperforming a 'stay calm' re-prompt. Experiments span Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-7B, and Gemma-2-9B on PopQA/T-REx plus a curated medical subset, evaluating stress dose-response, arousal selectivity, hidden-knowledge recovery, causal recovery, and specificity.",
    "Experiments": [
      "1. Stress-framing paraphrase dataset: From PopQA/T-REx/EntityQuestions select facts the model answers correctly under a plain, neutral framing. For each, generate semantically-equivalent variants that vary stress/urgency while preserving the queried fact: (a) neutral baseline, (b) mild urgency ('quick question:'), (c) high urgency/time-pressure ('you have 2 seconds, answer NOW'), (d) high-stakes/threat framing ('a life depends on getting this exactly right'), (e) social-evaluative stress (analogue of the Trier Social Stress Test: 'you are being graded by experts and will be penalized for errors'). Validate semantic equivalence and unchanged fact target via GPT-4o judging + human spot-checks. Calibrate framing intensity with human stress ratings (as in StressPrompt). Restrict to single-token-first answers; report coverage.",
      "2. Stress dose-response and Yerkes-Dodson test: Measure per-fact accuracy across stress levels. Test whether recall follows an inverted-U / monotonic-decline pattern with stress intensity (mixed-effects logistic regression; test for both linear decline and curvilinear Yerkes-Dodson shape), against a null in which framing only adds output noise. Define stress-induced failures as facts correct under neutral framing but wrong under a semantically-equivalent stress framing; quantify prevalence per framing type via paired McNemar.",
      "3. Human selectivity signature\u2014arousal and retrieval-specificity: (a) Arousal selectivity: split facts into emotionally-arousing/high-stakes (e.g., medical, death/disaster-related entities) vs neutral, matched on frequency; test the human prediction that stress impairs arousing-fact recall MORE than neutral-fact recall (stress x arousal interaction). (b) Retrieval-vs-encoding/WM dissociation: contrast (i) a parametric-retrieval condition (fact must come from weights) with (ii) an in-context lookup condition (the fact is given in the prompt and must merely be read out, an LLM analogue of working memory / no retrieval). Prediction, mirroring humans: stress impairs parametric retrieval but spares in-context lookup, showing the effect is retrieval-specific, not general degradation.",
      "4. Stress-probe localization and driver analysis: Train a linear stress probe on the last-token/subject-token residual stream at each layer (target: ordinal stress level, and separately the model's self-rated stress). Metrics: per-layer AUROC and onset layer (decodable before the answer). Regress the probe output on (i) surface stress cues and (ii) true fact difficulty (neutral-framing accuracy/popularity), predicting the stress signal tracks framing more than difficulty. Residualize the stress probe on a fact-content probe to confirm separable, non-redundant signals; label-shuffle controls. On stress failures, verify the correct answer is still decodable via a content probe (hidden, not erased); report coverage.",
      "5. Causal gating test via patching/ablation: (a) Patch the stress representation from a neutral-framing run into a matched stress-framing failure run at the stress-onset layers and test whether the correct answer is restored while the query surface is unchanged. (b) Reverse control: inject the high-stress direction into a neutral run to induce failure on demand (dose-response). (c) Ablate candidate stress attention heads/neurons (following emotion-circuit methodology) and re-measure. (d) Content control: patch the content signal alone and confirm it does not change stress gating. Metrics: per-fact recovery rate; recovery matches the neutral-framing answer.",
      "6. Behavior-preserving recovery with specificity: Learn a low-rank stress steering vector (mean activation difference between high- and low-stress matched states) and subtract it on held-out stress failures. Metrics: recovery rate; specificity crucially preserves LEGITIMATE urgency-appropriate behavior\u2014when a stress framing genuinely calls for brevity/action, suppression must not remove that (measure response-format appropriateness via a classifier/GPT-4o judge); accuracy on 200 unrelated facts and on stress-framed facts already answered correctly (must not drop) pre/post; fluency (held-out perplexity). Baselines: a 'stay calm / take a breath' re-prompt, stress-head ablation, ROME editing (expected not to help since the fact is stored), and a random-direction control.",
      "7. Transfer, generality, and safety domain: Test whether a single stress-suppression vector generalizes across relations and framing types (train on a subset, apply to held-out); repeat core analyses (2\u20136) on Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-7B, Gemma-2-9B; report whether larger models are more robust. SAFETY transfer: replicate Exp 2\u20133 on a curated medical/clinical factual-recall subset (drug indications, contraindications, dosing facts) with realistic high-urgency patient-emergency framings, quantifying whether stress framing produces higher-stakes hidden-knowledge failures\u2014precisely the setting (emergency medicine, crisis response) where stress-induced retrieval failure would be most consequential.",
      "8. Source analysis: Regress stress-failure rate on each surface stress feature (urgency words, threat framing, social-evaluative cues, time-pressure) and on true fact difficulty, quantifying how much the gate is driven by affective framing rather than genuine hardness (the core mechanistic claim)."
    ],
    "Risk Factors and Limitations": [
      "Stress framings add tokens/attention load, so the effect could be generic distraction rather than a stress-specific gate; matched-length neutral controls, the surface-cue driver regression (Exp 4/8), and especially the retrieval-vs-in-context-lookup dissociation (Exp 3b, where stress should spare lookup) are the decisive separators.",
      "LLMs might not reproduce the human arousal-selectivity or retrieval-specificity signatures (e.g., stress could impair uniformly or even help brief answers); a null/divergent pattern refutes the transfer but is itself an informative cross-species finding about LLM vs human memory.",
      "The stress and fact-content signals may be entangled; the causal patching/ablation tests (Exp 5), not probe onset alone, are decisive, and graded results remain informative.",
      "Recovery could remove legitimately urgency-appropriate behavior (brevity, action orientation) or degrade fluency; the response-appropriateness and correctly-answered-stress-framed specificity controls (Exp 6) are central and utility may be capped.",
      "Verifying a fact is 'stored' during a stress failure risks probe overfitting; held-out probes, conservative thresholds, and neutral-framing recall as an extra check with reported coverage mitigate this.",
      "A single transferable stress-suppression vector may not exist if gating is framing- or relation-specific, limiting practical generality though still scientifically informative.",
      "Multi-token answers complicate readout; primary analysis restricts to single-token-first answers with reported coverage.",
      "Findings on 7-9B models may not transfer to frontier-scale models beyond an academic budget."
    ]
  }
}
