s impairs parametric retrieval but spares in-context lookup, showing the effect is retrieval-specific, not general degradation.', "4. Stress-probe localization and driver analysis: Train a linear stress probe on the last-token/subject-token residual stream at each layer (target: ordinal stress level, and separately the model's self-rated stress). Metrics: per-layer AUROC and onset layer (decodable before the answer). Regress the probe output on (i) surface stress cues and (ii) true fact difficulty (neutral-framing accuracy/popularity), predicting the stress signal tracks framing more than difficulty. Residualize the stress probe on a fact-content probe to confirm separable, non-redundant signals; label-shuffle controls. On stress failures, verify the correct answer is still decodable via a content probe (hidden, not erased); report coverage.", '5. Causal gating test via patching/ablation: (a) Patch the stress representation from a neutral-framing run into a matched stress-framing failure run at the stress-onset layers and test whether the correct answer is restored while the query surface is unchanged. (b) Reverse control: inject the high-stress direction into a neutral run to induce failure on demand (dose-response). (c) Ablate candidate stress attention heads/neurons (following emotion-circuit methodology) and re-measure. (d) Content control: patch the content signal alone and confirm it does not change stress gating. Metrics: per-fact recovery rate; recovery matches the neutral-framing answer.', "6. Behavior-preserving recovery with specificity: Learn a low-rank stress steering vector (mean activation difference between high- and low-stress matched states) and subtract it on held-out stress failures. Metrics: recovery rate; specificity crucially preserves LEGITIMATE urgency-appropriate behavior—when a stress framing genuinely calls for brevity/action, suppression must not remove that (measure response-format appropriateness via a classifier/GPT-4o judge); accuracy on 200 unrelated facts and on stress-framed facts already answered correctly (must not drop) pre/post; fluency (held-out perplexity). Baselines: a 'stay calm / take a breath' re-prompt, stress-head ablation, ROME editing (expected not to help since the fact is stored), and a random-direction control.", '7. Transfer, generality, and safety domain: Test whether a single stress-suppression vector generalizes across relations and framing types (train on a subset, apply to held-out); repeat core analyses (2–6) on Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-7B, Gemma-2-9B; report whether larger models are more robust. SAFETY transfer: replicate Exp 2–3 on a curated medical/clinical factual-recall subset (drug indications, contraindications, dosing facts) with realistic high-urgency patient-emergency framings, quantifying whether stress framing produces higher-stakes hidden-knowledge failures—precisely the setting (emergency medicine, crisis response) where stress-induced retrieval failure would be most consequential.', '8. Source analysis: Regress stress-failure rate on each surface stress feature (urgency words, threat framing, social-evaluative cues, time-pressure) and on true fact difficulty, quantifying how much the gate is driven by affective framing rather than genuine hardness (the core mechanistic claim).'], 'Risk Factors and Limitations': ['Stress framings add tokens/attention load, so the effect could be generic distraction rather than a stress-specific gate; matched-length neutral controls, the surface-cue driver regression (Exp 4/8), and especially the retrieval-vs-in-context-lookup dissociation (Exp 3b, where stress should spare lookup) are the decisive separators.', 'LLMs might not reproduce the human arousal-selectivity or retrieval-specificity signatures (e.g., stress could impair uniformly or even help brief answers); a null/divergent pattern refutes the transfer but is itself an informative cross-species finding about LLM vs human memory.', 'The stress and fact-content signal