istributional certainty, testing the selective-accessibility prediction (accessibility scales with anchor properties) against a pure distributional-certainty account. Per-layer AUROC of the signal predicting anchored error; label-shuffle controls.", '5. Causal test via patching/steering: (a) Patch the pre-anchor (no-anchor) residual representation into an anchored-error run at the identified layers and test whether the un-anchored correct value is restored. (b) Suppress the learned anchor-accessibility direction and re-measure assimilation. (c) Reverse control: inject the accessibility direction (or a synthetic anchor signal) into a no-anchor run to induce assimilation on demand (dose-response). (d) Content control: patch the fact-content signal alone and confirm it does not change the anchoring pattern. Metrics: per-fact recovery rate; sign and dose-response.', "6. De-anchoring intervention with specificity: Learn a low-rank anchor-accessibility steering vector and subtract it on held-out anchored queries. Metrics: reduction in assimilation / recovery of un-anchored accuracy; specificity (accuracy on no-anchor facts and on cases where the anchor is legitimately informative must not degrade; accuracy on 200 unrelated facts pre/post); fluency (held-out perplexity). Baselines: 'ignore the previous number / answer independently' re-prompt, chain-of-thought, authority-bias-style residual steering, ROME editing (expected not to help since the fact is stored), and a random-direction control.", '7. Transfer and generality: Test whether a single de-anchoring vector generalizes across relations and anchor types (train on a subset, apply to held-out); repeat core analyses (2-6) on Llama-3-8B, Qwen2.5-7B, Gemma-2-9B; report whether larger models resist anchoring via stronger fact-content signals.', '8. Safety-domain transfer: Replicate Exp 2-5 on curated clinical numeric facts (drug dosages, lab reference ranges) where an incidental anchor (e.g., a mentioned dose for a different drug) could shift a stored correct value, quantifying whether anchor-driven retrieval contamination produces higher-stakes numeric errors than in general-knowledge prompts.'], 'Risk Factors and Limitations': ['Anchoring could be pure output-distribution imitation with no retrieval contamination; the hidden-knowledge probe (Exp 3) and the induce-on-demand causal test (Exp 5c) are the decisive separators, and a null here would refute the selective-accessibility framing while remaining informative.', 'The anchor-accessibility and fact-content signals may be entangled, especially since both live in numeric-magnitude subspaces (per Multi-Attribute Confounding 2025); the causal patching/steering tests, not probe AUROC alone, are decisive, and graded results remain informative.', 'Distinguishing selective accessibility from the distributional-certainty account (Owusu 2026) is subtle; the driver regression (Exp 4) that separates anchor-property scaling from un-anchored certainty is the key test, but the two may partly coincide.', 'De-anchoring could over-correct on cases where the anchor is legitimately relevant, or degrade fluency; the informative-anchor and no-anchor specificity controls (Exp 6) are central and utility may be capped.', 'Multi-token numeric readout complicates probing/logit-lens; primary analysis uses log-magnitude probes and tolerance-band accuracy rather than exact-digit recovery, with reported coverage.', 'A single transferable de-anchoring vector may not exist if accessibility is relation- or anchor-type-specific, limiting practical generality though still scientifically informative.', 'Findings on 7-9B models may not transfer to frontier-scale models beyond an academic budget.']}

